+# CHK001 — pin flow, end to end
+
+Run: 2026-09-27, release build of this branch, against a **fresh scratch
+database** (`WORKLOG_HOME` in the job tmp dir) — the live database was not
+read or written. Scratch daemon on `127.0.0.1:9423`, scratch `next dev` on
+`127.0.0.1:3123` pointed at it.
+
+Checkout: `~/Desktop/Work/vitinn-infra/.claude/worktrees/fix-ci-ecr-pull`
+(branch `fix/code-interpreter-ecr-pull-through`, not a default branch).
+Registry: `vitinn-infra` marked multi-tenant; seeded customers incl. Sjúkra, APRÓ.
+
+## Steps and results
+
+1. Session A start — `worklog session-hint` with SessionStart JSON (cwd = the
+   checkout) printed the instruction, exit 0 → `CHK001-hint-session-a.txt`.
+2. Session A pins Sjúkra — row inserted exactly as `worklog pin Sjúkra
+   --session chk-sess-a` stores it (source `claude`, folder `vitinn-infra`,
+   branch above). The command itself could not be run with that cwd from this
+   isolated session; its storage is covered by `pin_stores_a_known_customer`.
+3. Session B start on the same branch (the `/clear` + `/flow:next` case) —
+   `worklog session-hint` printed "This session is for Sjúkra (pinned from
+   branch fix/code-interpreter-ecr-pull-through)…", exit 0, and stored an
+   `inherited` pin for chk-sess-b → `CHK001-hint-session-b.txt`.
+4. Synthetic work on 2026-09-28: A 09:00–09:38, B 10:00–10:38, and a third
+   session C 11:00–11:38 whose text names APRÓ. `worklog infer --day
+   2026-09-28` → 2 blocks: 09:00–10:55 (A+B), 10:55–11:40 (C).
+5. `GET /blocks/1/customer-slices` → `Sjúkra`, origin `pinned`;
+   `/blocks/2/customer-slices` → `APRÓ`, origin `fallback`.
+6. Day view: block 1 shows "Sjúkra · pinned · Change"; block 2 "APRÓ · guess ·
+   Change" → `CHK001-day-view.png`. Block detail view of block 1 shows
